    "title": "1 man shot to death inside a vehicle Wednesday in midtown Kansas City, Missouri - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KSHB 41 News Staff ,\n6 hours ago One man was shot to death Wednesday afternoon while in his vehicle in Midtown Kansas City, Missouri.\nPolice were sent at 4:30 p.m. on a report of gunshots fired at Linwood and Broadway boulevards.\nOfficers found the victim unresponsive inside his vehicle. He was declared dead a short time later at a hospital.\nPeople who called police about the shooting and people at the shooting scene told officers the victim was inside his vehicle when another vehicle pulled next to the victim's vehicle.\nPolice said shots appeared to have been fired from the vehicle that pulled next to the victim's vehicle.\nNo description of the suspect or their vehicle have been released.\nThe victim's name has not been released.\nChris Morrison/KSHB 41 KCPD investigating homicide at Linwood, Broadway boulevards This was the eighth homicide of the year in KCMO, compared to 11 homicides at this time last year in the city.\n—\nIf you have any information about a crime, you may contact your local police department directly. But if you want or need to remain anonymous, you should contact the Greater Kansas City Crime Stoppers Tips Hotline by calling 816-474-TIPS (8477), submitting the tip online or through the free mobile app at P3Tips.com . Depending on your tip, Crime Stoppers could offer you a cash reward.\nAnnual homicide details and data for the Kansas City area are available through the KSHB 41 News Homicide Tracker , which was launched in 2015. Read the KSHB 41 News Mug Shot Policy .\n6",
